# Mobile workspace is required

Every terrain-desk and building-desk feature must remain usable on phones and tablets.

## Supported viewports

- Verify at least 360×640 and 390×844 portrait, 844×390 landscape, 768×1024 tablet, and a desktop viewport.
- Use `viewport-fit=cover`, safe-area insets, `visualViewport`, and the shared `web/mobile-workspace.css` / `web/mobile-workspace.js` infrastructure.
- Never disable browser zoom with `maximum-scale` or `user-scalable=no`.

## Interaction

- Primary touch targets are at least 44×44 CSS pixels.
- Canvas interaction uses Pointer Events and pointer capture. One finger operates the active tool; two fingers pan and zoom without leaving an accidental edit.
- Every hover-only action needs an always-visible or tap-accessible equivalent.
- Sheets and dialogs must trap focus, restore focus, close with Escape, and keep the covered workspace inert.

## Layout

- The canvas remains the main workspace. Phone portrait uses bottom navigation plus bottom sheets; phone landscape/tablet may use a side sheet.
- Do not hard-code layout from `window.innerHeight`; use the shared visual viewport variables.
- Inputs use at least 16px text on mobile to prevent unwanted browser zoom.
- Preserve game coordinate systems, export formats, building UID mappings, and the locked building frame. Mobile adaptation changes viewport chrome, not native rendering geometry.
